  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the three planes<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Then, which one of the following is true?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
